{
  // Scoped typecheck project for the package's whole `test/` tree. `check-types`
  // runs this as a SECOND `tsc` pass (after the composite `tsc -b`), because the
  // composite build emits declarations only for `src` and never sees `test/**`.
  //
  // `@alfred/integrations` used to be the one package whose tests NO CI job ran.
  // The `leaf-db-tests` job now runs them, so this pass is no longer the only
  // automated reader of the tree — but it stays the only reader of the TYPES.
  // Until this project existed nothing read these files at all: a type error, or
  // an `import type` from a module that no longer exists, survived
  // `pnpm check-types` at exit 0 and no test run contradicted it.
  //
  // `include` covers `test` rather than any narrower glob so that a file added
  // anywhere under `test/` is type-checked without an edit here. That matches
  // the `tsx --test "test/**/*.test.ts"` runner glob, so a new file joins both
  // sets at once.
  //
  // The base `tsconfig.json` is `composite: true`; a `tsc -p` invocation with
  // `noEmit` errors unless `composite`/`declaration` are overridden off here.
  // Nothing under `test/` is emitted or built — this project only type-checks.
  //
  // `exclude` is a BASELINE, not a policy. Both entries arrived with the files
  // themselves, which moved here from `packages/api/test/` and carried their two
  // entries out of that project's list — the repo total does not move. They read
  // a `SealedCredentialSecret` as a `string`, which the branded symbol type
  // refuses; the diagnostics are real debt in the assertions, not an artifact of
  // the move, and the relative-import rewrite was measured NOT to resolve them.
  // `pnpm check:test-typecheck-baseline` derives this list from `tsc` and fails
  // when it drifts in either direction: an entry whose file is now clean or
  // absent must be deleted, and a file that is dirty and unlisted must be
  // repaired. Paths are literal on purpose — a directory glob would silently
  // un-check every file added tomorrow.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".",
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": false
  },
  "include": ["src", "test"],
  "exclude": ["test/credential-persistence.test.ts", "test/google-credential-refresh.test.ts"]
}
